-- title:
--   Properness of a ↦ σ(a)a⁻¹ modulo K_∞^×
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite extension of $K$ that is Galois over $K$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$; thus $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$. Write $K_\infty$ for `InfiniteAdeleRing K` and $E = L \otimes_K K_\infty$, and let $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$ denote the ring endomorphism [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaTensor K L (InfiniteAdeleRing K) σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L199) of $E$ obtained from $\sigma$ on the left factor and the identity on $K_\infty$. The assertion is: for every compact subset $C$ of the unit group $E^\times$ there is a compact subset $C'$ of $E^\times$ with the following property. For every $a \in E^\times$ such that the twisted quotient $(\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(a) \cdot a^{-1}$, formed via the induced map on units, lies in $C$, there exists a unit $p$ of $K_\infty$ whose image $1 \otimes p$ under the unit map induced by `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` satisfies $(1 \otimes p) \cdot a \in C'$.
--
--   This is the properness, modulo $K_\infty^\times$, of the twisting map $a \mapsto \sigma(a)a^{-1}$ on the units of $L \otimes_K K_\infty$: whose kernel is exactly $1 \otimes K_\infty^\times$ by Hilbert's theorem 90 for the cyclic extension $L/K$, so that a compact set of twisted quotients is covered by a compact set of representatives. It is used in the archimedean convergence estimate [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_lintegral_mul_indicator_mul_sigmaTensor_mul_inv_le_of_isCompact`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_lintegral_mul_indicator_mul_sigmaTensor_mul_inv_le_of_isCompact) for twisted orbital integrals.
